If a patient has an age and the age includes at least 65 years and a clinician initiates an opioid for the patient then the clinician should initiate the opioid cautiously for the patient.
If a patient has a renal-insufficiency and a clinician initiates an opioid for the patient then the clinician should initiate the opioid cautiously for the patient.
If a patient has a hepatic-insufficiency and a clinician initiates an opioid for the patient then the clinician should initiate the opioid cautiously for the patient.
